      "writtenOn": "2021-02-26T20:59:43Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think to avoid polling too much. What we have in platform/ec is the console_buffer logic is the one that polls the uart then stores things into the buffer. I actually think that in the Zephyr code we could use Zephyr\u0027s event signals to do this a bit better, this way we:\n1. Fork the RX from the shell using a new API we\u0027ll introduce to the shell_uart upstream.\n2. Update our console_buffer to use the forked callback to fill a buffer and signal an event when data is available.\n3. Here instead of waiting, listen for the signal and grab the byte.\n\n* I\u0027ll add this detail to the bug that Keith asked me to open on this.",
      "parentUuid": "1546c71e_ad739d72",
